ng script fixture values remain unchanged, and make validate plus make regenerate-check pass.\"); set_details(TASK-260720-1673lr, title=\"Consume the shared compiled-build suite in Curator\", description=\"Add an independent Go consumer for every shared compiled-build interoperability case. The consumer must exercise Curator behavior against the external suite root and derive no expected values from csk or from implementation-local fixtures.\", scope=\"Work in the Curator repository after the Curator Go build-driver story and TASK-260720-2g7avf. Own focused tests and test-only helpers under the existing external conformance surface, using CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT. Exercise real manifest parsing, install planning, build and cache behavior, shim launch, argument and exit propagation, and rejection ordering in isolated temporary homes and projects. Do not call or import csk, copy shared vectors into the repository, weaken no-skip behavior, or change the curator-spec CI pin in this task.\", ac=\"With CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT set, the Go consumer enumerates every shared compiled-build case exactly once and fails on unknown, missing, duplicate, or skipped case IDs. The positive fixture installs from the unmodified suite, excludes build roots from context and runtime copies, builds on a miss, reuses a verified cache entry, performs a compiler-free and mutation-free dry-run, and launches the installed command with the exact shared stdout, stderr, forwarded arguments, and exit status. Every shared negative case is rejected in the expected normalized class and at the required before-build or before-mutation boundary. Test homes, project roots, Go caches, and subprocess recording are isolated per case; no implementation-owned expected outcome or binary hash is introduced. The focused external-suite tests and go test ./... pass when the suite is supplied, while developer runs may skip only when the environment variable is absent.\"); set_details(TASK-260720-31zeo2, title=\"Consume the shared compiled-build suite in csk\", description=\"Add an independent Python consumer for every shared compiled-build interoperability case. The consumer must exercise csk behavior against the external suite root and derive no expected values from Curator or from implementation-local fixtures.\", scope=\"Work in the csk repository after the csk Go build-driver story and TASK-260720-2g7avf. Own focused tests and test-only helpers in the existing protocol conformance surface, using CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT. Exercise real manifest parsing, install planning, build and cache behavior, shim launch, argument and exit propagation, and rejection ordering in isolated temporary homes and projects. Do not call or import Curator, copy shared vectors into the repository, weaken no-skip behavior, or change the curator-spec CI pin in this task.\", ac=\"With CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT set, the Python consumer parametrizes every shared compiled-build case exactly once and fails on unknown, missing, duplicate, xfailed, or skipped case IDs. The positive fixture installs from the unmodified suite, excludes build roots from context and runtime copies, builds on a miss, reuses a verified cache entry, performs a compiler-free and mutation-free dry-run including audit-registry state, and launches the installed command with the exact shared stdout, stderr, forwarded arguments, and exit status. Every shared negative case is rejected in the expected normalized class and at the required before-build or before-mutation boundary. Test homes, project roots, Go caches, and subprocess recording are isolated per case; no implementation-owned expected outcome or binary hash is introduced. The focused external-suite tests, full pytest suite, and strict type check pass when the suite is supplied, while developer runs may skip only when the environment variable is absent.\"); set_details(TASK-260720-3nj1r6, title=\"Run both managers through one black-box interoperability gate\", description=\"Add a curator-spec-owned runner that invokes the two independent conformance entrypoints against the same immutable suite root and compares their normalized case results without importing either implementation.\", scope=\"Work in curator-spec after TASK-260720-1673lr and TASK-260720-31zeo2. Own a tools entrypoint, its unit tests, and concise operator documentation. Accept explicit Curator and csk checkout or executable paths plus the suite root; create separate temporary manager homes, projects, caches, and fixture copies; emit one machine-readable result record per case. The suite remains the oracle. Do not embed manager refs, release pins, copied expected values, implementation-specific cache layouts, or cross-manager code imports.\", ac=\"The runner validates the suite manifest before execution, invokes each manager consumer with the identical suite bytes, and rejects missing, extra, duplicate, skipped, xfailed, timed-out, or crashed cases. Its normalization removes only declared transport differences such as temporary absolute paths and platform executable suffixes; acceptance or rejection class, build or no-build boundary, mutation class, launch stdout and stderr, forwarded arguments, and exit status remain comparable. The two managers run in disjoint state roots and never consume one another’s cache or artifacts. A JSON report identifies suite digest, implementation identities supplied by the caller, per-case outcomes, and parity verdict without claiming release conformance. Unit tests inject divergent, missing, skipped, timeout, and malformed result streams and prove the runner fails closed. The documented local command succeeds against qualified checkouts and curator-spec validation remains green.\"); set_details(TASK-260720-14jjgt, title=\"Publish the portable compiled-skill authoring guide\", description=\"Publish a practical implementation-neutral guide for authors of schema v6 Go command skills, building on the normative schema and CLI documentation without 